===Etymology 1===
Proposed to be derived from {{inh|yo|alv-yor-pro|*o-ríɣo}}, {{m|alv-yor-pro|*o-rí}}, from {{inh|yo|alv-edk-pro|*o-ríɣo}}, {{m|alv-edk-pro|*o-rí}}, ultimately from {{inh|yo|alv-yrd-pro|*ó-ɗí}}, {{m|alv-yrd-pro|*ó-dí}}. Cognate with {{cog|igl|ójí}}. The compounding of the suffix "ɣo" (later "wo") is possibly an Proto-Edekiri innovation still maintained in a majority of Edekiri languages, and the non-suffixed version likely existed side by side. However, {{cog|aye|ago}} may suggest it is a remnant of an older root. See potential non-Yoruboid cognates, {{cog|aqg|egírí|igíri}}, {{cog|bnt-pro|*mʊ̀tʊ́è}}, {{cog|nic-grf-pro|*tú}}, {{cog|nic-plt-pro|*-tii}}, {{cog|nic-bco-pro|*-to}}, possibly {{cog|ig|isi}}, {{cog|ibe|ìcùm}}, perhaps ultimately from {{inh|yo|alv-pro|*-li-}} or {{inh|yo|nic-pro|*-túi}}, {{m|nic-pro|*-tu}}

Cognate with {{cog|idd|erío}}, {{cog|ife|eríwo}}, {{cog|ulb|órí}}, and {{cog|its|orígho}}.

